    <string name="map_layer_wifi_count_heatmap_description">Shows how many distinct access points overlap at each place. Repeated scans of the same AP count once, so hotter areas mean genuinely denser radio coverage.</string>
    <string name="map_layer_wifi_heatmap_description">A band-aware Wi-Fi constellation from your own observations. Colored fields show observed 2.4, 5, and 6 GHz coverage; glowing centers are approximate AP positions shown only when the sample geometry supports them.</string>
